  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: The two strongest signals from 5 experiments are (1) scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 for RNA encoding (+7.1% acc, config_021 vs config_001) and (2) transformer > avgpool for aggregation (+1.9% acc, config_049 vs config_021). The current best (config_049: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.7250 acc at only 3.60 GPU hrs. The key remaining uncertainty is whether scgpt could outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder — both are learned encoders but with different architectures, and no scgpt+transformer+weighted combination has been tested yet. config_043 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean A/B test against config_049, changing only the RNA encoder while holding all other parameters at their best-known values. If scgpt wins, we get a new best; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can focus remaining budget on finer-tuning other dimensions. Expected cost: similar to config_049 (~4–6 GPU hrs) since scgpt is a learned encoder of comparable complexity to scvi_n200, and the transformer aggregation + ViT-L image encoder are the same. This is the highest-information experiment available: it resolves the most impactful untested design choice while preserving all known best settings."
